{{- /*
  What a secret scan is allowed to print about a finding (issue #1288).

  Every CPP entry point to gitleaks - `make secret-scan`, the CI secret-scan
  step, scripts/secret-scan-check.sh and tests/test_secret_scan.py - renders its
  findings through THIS template instead of `--verbose`. Verbose output prints
  each finding's Match and Secret, and `--redact` cannot make that safe: it masks
  each finding's OWN secret only, so a value inside ANOTHER rule's match (a PAT
  inside a curl-auth-header line) was printed in full, and in colour mode the
  surrounding source line leaked too. Both were reproduced on the pinned v8.30.1.

  So the scanner is asked for metadata alone: rule, file, line. The `RuleID:`
  prefix is load-bearing - the negative control and the tests count those lines.
  Do not add Match, Secret, Line content or Fingerprint-with-content here.
*/ -}}
{{- range . }}RuleID: {{ .RuleID }}
File: {{ .File }}
Line: {{ .StartLine }}

{{ end -}}
